## What shipped
Ported all **3 web hooks** from `useSettingsBackup.ts` to UI-free KMP shared-core state holders:

| Web hook | KMP surface | Endpoint |
|---|---|---|
| `useExportSettings` | `SettingsBackupStore.exportSettings()` | `GET /settings/export` |
| `useDryRunImport` | `dryRunImport(bundle)` | `POST /settings/import {dry_run:true, bundle}` |
| `useApplyImport` | `applyImport(bundle)` | `POST /settings/import {dry_run:false, bundle}` |

**Key parity decisions:**
- The domain has **0 reads** (all `useMutation`, no `useQuery`), so no `Resource` feed/CacheDomain ΓÇö instead the hooks' `setQueryData(lastExport/lastImport)` priming is reproduced as observable `StateFlow<SettingsBundle?>`/`StateFlow<SettingsImportResult?>`, updated only on success.
- Bundle nested verbatim under `bundle`; opaque sections round-trip shape-preserving; null sections dropped (`JSON.stringify`/`explicitNulls=false`).
- SUDO step-up handled transparently by the shared client (no bespoke plumbing).
- `downloadSettingsBundle` correctly excluded (browser-only Blob/DOM side effect).

**Derivations** (golden-vectored for KMP+C# parity): `defaultExportFilename` (UTC `YYYYMMDD`) and `summariseImportResult` (`total = added+updated`, skipped excluded).

